{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"0705b94c419f193bab4f95adbb386f52e43776cb75d35af4efd272479fcb36d8","digest":{"component_or_area":"security detector loader and YAML validation","key_entities":["test_code_review_ws5.py","src/rebar/grounding/detectors/registry","load_registry()","_detectors_from_file()","security_iac_public_exposure.yaml","security_owasp_cwe.yaml","security_secrets_gitleaks.yaml","Detector","_detector_from_rule()"],"problem_keywords":["security rule validation","yaml parsing","detector loading","fail-closed behavior","malformed data","rule contract"],"propositions":["Current substring/presence-only test does not validate actual detector id/backend/severity contract loaded by production registry; replacement must assert exact detector ids, backends, and severities for each of the three security families via load_registry()","Invalid YAML in a vendored security-rule file must yield zero detectors and a recorded parse_error reason when loaded via _detectors_from_file(), ensuring malformed data fails closed and observable","A security rule missing its id field must be silently skipped per-rule (absent from returned detectors) while sibling well-formed rules in the same file still load, with no parse_drops entry created for the per-rule skip","The fail-closed loader behavior (both file-level invalid YAML and rule-level missing id) must be tested through _detectors_from_file() against temporary malformed fixtures, not via hand-parsed YAML"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785820439484553125,"uuid":"e1d0feb5-7eca-4110-84ee-0661db28df65"}